===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|haddok}}, from {{der|en|xno|hadoc}}, from {{der|en|fro|hadot}}.  Further origin uncertain, but {{m|fro|hadot}} could have evolved from {{m|fro|(h)adoux}}, {{m|fro|(h)adoz}}, from {{m|fro|adoub}}, from {{m|fro|adouber}}, {{m|fro|adober||to prepare}}, cognate with {{cog|it|addobbare||to [[souse]] fish or meat}}.<ref>Weekley, Ernest (2013): An Etymological Dictionary of Modern English</ref>

The spelling is usually regarded as a diminutive in {{m|enm|-ok}} (see {{l|en|-ock}}).

